                <pb facs="0286" n="216" sameAs="frus:frus1934v04/pg216"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/4148: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Des Portes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-09-19T15:00:00-04:00">September 19, 1934—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>63. Department’s telegram No. 22.<anchor n="43" xml:id="d268-f1"/> The message
                    was delivered orally to the Minister of Foreign Affairs this afternoon.</p>
                <p>He expressed regret that the United States and Brazil will not form part of a
                    committee appointed by the League; and stated that when the pause is ended he
                    hopes the United States and Brazil will continue the negotiations. He expressed
                    the wish that the United States would take the initiative in such negotiations
                    to avoid such a situation as has occurred with the Argentine initiative.</p>
                <p>He stated he plans to keep the United States informed of developments.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Des Portes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
